title: Add opt-in app-server-backed Codex session launcher
---
Depends on P1.M1.E1.T001 proving the protocol.

Add an explicitly experimental c2c launch mode that starts a local app-server on a private Unix socket and runs interactive Codex as `codex --remote unix://PATH`. Keep the ordinary `c2c start codex` path unchanged.

Acceptance criteria:
- Private socket location, lifecycle ownership, cleanup, and restart behavior are deterministic.
- Never expose a TCP listener by default; remote TCP requires explicit operator configuration and documented auth.
- Persist the mapping between c2c session identity, app-server endpoint, and Codex thread id without leaking message contents.
- Clearly report unavailable/unsupported Codex versions.
- The launcher has fixture-gated tests plus a real tmux dogfood launch.

Blockers: P1.M1.E1.T001 go decision and protocol observations.